# Admin dashboard — out of scope by default

Treat the **admin dashboard** as a separate concern from the main trip-planner app.

## Unless the user clearly says they are working on the admin dashboard

Do **not** proactively:

- Open, edit, or search under `src/app/admin/`
- Open or edit `src/server/repos/admin.ts`
- Open or edit `src/app/api/admin/`

Use minimal context from those areas when answering questions about the **main** app (trips, vehicles, Penny, auth flows, etc.). Prefer `schema.ts`, trip repos, and shared libs instead—even if an answer could mention admin aggregates.

## When this rule does **not** apply

If the user explicitly scopes admin work, e.g. they mention **admin dashboard**, **`/admin`**, **admin errors/users/chats pages**, or **“we’re working on admin”**, then use those paths normally.

## Not admin-only (always in play)

- `src/server/auth/admin.ts` — allowlist helper used across the app; not part of the “dashboard” exclusion.
